    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offensive engine is anchored today by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our highest efficiency score of 80.62. His matchup against Kirby is dampened by the pitcher\u2019s skill, but the combination of a favorable hitter\u2019s park and a high-leverage opportunity to exploit a slow delivery makes him a priority start for stolen base potential. **Jackson Merrill** follows closely with a 75.27 rating; he benefits from a strong platoon advantage against Singer and favorable wind conditions, positioning him as the primary catalyst in the lineup. **Kyle Tucker** (64.73) remains a rock-solid play despite a tougher matchup, as his efficiency holds steady regardless of the opposing arm.\n\nDecisions in the middle of the order reflect a calculated approach to platoon splits and game flow. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (60.44) and **Josh Jung** (60.24) represent our strongest mid-tier assets, though **Josh Jung** carries a 39% rain risk that bears watching throughout the afternoon. Our most difficult roster call was moving **Miguel Vargas** (42.64) to the bench; while he remained in consideration, the optimizer favored the higher-ceiling platoon edges provided by **Nasim Nunez** (56.32) and **Wade Meckler** (52.67), whose favorable SP matchups against Ray and Lambert outweighed the risk of starting **Miguel Vargas** against a high-skill arm like Sale.\n\nWe are monitoring the bottom of the order closely, specifically **Brayan Rocchio** (46.63) and **Dominic Smith** (49.53), as both sit near the marginal threshold. Their spots in the lineup are kept to preserve our game caps while ensuring we remain competitive in volume. While we are effectively managing the IR slots occupied by **Jordan Westburg** and **Jorge Polanco**, the active roster remains focused on maximizing efficiency for our daily rotation. With **Liam Hicks** (56.60) holding down the C1 spot, we are positioned to capitalize on favorable platoon matchups across the board, provided the weather in **Josh Jung**\u2019s stadium holds steady.",
